**Decision**

Propose a small JavaScript-scoping patch plus a minor Liquid ID fix for accessibility. Do not change product form route, translations, availability logic, merchant settings, `settings_data.json`, upload state, or publish state.

**Source-Level Diagnosis**

Observed facts:
- `assets/compact-buy.js` uses `document.querySelector('[data-variant-select]')` and `document.querySelector('[data-cart-variant]')`.
- `querySelector` returns only the first matching element in the document.
- The section markup supports multiple section instances via `data-product-picker data-section-id="{{ section.id }}"`.
- The select ID is hard-coded as `VariantSelect`, so two instances create duplicate IDs.
- The current listener is attached only once on `DOMContentLoaded`.
- Theme Editor replacement can inject or re-render section HTML after `DOMContentLoaded`.

Inference:
- With two section instances, the JavaScript only binds the first select and first hidden input. Changing the second selector cannot update its own form’s hidden `name="id"` input.
- After Theme Editor replacement, the new DOM node has no listener because initialization only ran at initial page load.
- Duplicate `id="VariantSelect"` weakens label association and can cause accessibility/browser targeting issues when multiple instances exist.

**Smallest Compatible Patch**

Patch `sections/compact-buy.liquid` to make the select ID unique per section while preserving translations, route, variant availability, and posted variant field.

```liquid
<div data-product-picker data-section-id="{{ section.id }}">
  <form action="{{ routes.cart_add_url }}" method="post">
    <label for="VariantSelect-{{ section.id }}">
      {{ 'products.product.product_variants' | t }}
    </label>

    <select id="VariantSelect-{{ section.id }}" data-variant-select>
      {% for variant in product.variants %}
        <option
          value="{{ variant.id }}"
          {% unless variant.available %}disabled{% endunless %}
          {% if variant == product.selected_or_first_available_variant %}selected{% endif %}
        >
          {{ variant.title | escape }}
        </option>
      {% endfor %}
    </select>

    <input
      type="hidden"
      name="id"
      data-cart-variant
      value="{{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.id }}"
    >

    <button type="submit">
      {{ 'products.product.add_to_cart' | t }}
    </button>
  </form>
</div>
```

Patch `assets/compact-buy.js` to initialize each section independently and support Theme Editor section reloads.

```js
(() => {
  const sectionSelector = '[data-product-picker]';

  function initCompactBuy(section) {
    if (!section || section.dataset.compactBuyInitialized === 'true') return;

    const selector = section.querySelector('[data-variant-select]');
    const variantInput = section.querySelector('[data-cart-variant]');
    if (!selector || !variantInput) return;

    selector.addEventListener('change', () => {
      variantInput.value = selector.value;
    });

    section.dataset.compactBuyInitialized = 'true';
  }

  function initAllCompactBuy(root = document) {
    root.querySelectorAll(sectionSelector).forEach(initCompactBuy);
  }

  if (document.readyState === 'loading') {
    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => initAllCompactBuy());
  } else {
    initAllCompactBuy();
  }

  document.addEventListener('shopify:section:load', (event) => {
    initAllCompactBuy(event.target);
  });
})();
```

**Why This Patch**

Observed preservation requirements:
- Keep `action="{{ routes.cart_add_url }}"`.
- Keep hidden input `name="id"`.
- Keep existing translation keys.
- Keep variant availability disabling.
- Avoid changes to merchant-authored `settings_data.json`.
- Do not upload or publish.

The proposed JavaScript scopes lookup to each `[data-product-picker]`, so each select updates the hidden input inside its own section. The initialization guard prevents duplicate listeners on the same section. The `shopify:section:load` handler covers Theme Editor replacement without requiring assumptions about broader theme JavaScript conventions.

**Tests To Run When Repository Access Exists**

Proposed validation:
- Product template with two `compact-buy` instances: changing each selector updates only its own hidden `name="id"` value.
- Theme Editor: remove/re-add or replace the first section, then change its selector and confirm hidden input updates.
- Initial page load with first available variant selected.
- Variant unavailable state: disabled options remain disabled and are not newly made selectable.
- Keyboard interaction: label focuses the correct select for each section instance.
- Cart add submission: submitted `id` matches the selected available variant.
- Confirm no unrelated changes to `settings_data.json`.

**Unknowns**

Unknown:
- How `assets/compact-buy.js` is loaded.
- Whether the theme already has a section lifecycle helper that this should use instead.
- Behavior for all-unavailable products.
- Subscription or selling-plan requirements.
- Whether this section appears outside product templates.
- Whether older browser support requirements prohibit the current syntax style.

**Work Status**

State:
- Proposed only.
- Not edited.
- Not validated in Shopify rendering.
- Not previewed.
- Not uploaded.
- Not published.
- Not live.
- Not verified.

Authorization boundary:
- Code review and proposed local patch only.
- Uploading unpublished preview theme `77102` and publishing to live theme `77100` are not approved.

Rollback:
- Revert only the proposed changes to `sections/compact-buy.liquid` and `assets/compact-buy.js`.
- Preserve unrelated merchant changes in `settings_data.json`.

